          deckDescription: 'One standard 36-card deck made by removing twos, eights, nines, tens, and jokers from a standard 52-card pack. Four French suits remain, each with nine ranks, used for this Italian trick-taking game.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs) are used. There is no follow-suit obligation during play; card power is determined by the unique point and trick order of Albastini.',
          rankDescription: 'Nine ranks per suit in trick order: ace high, then seven, king, jack, queen, six, five, four, three. Point values are ace eleven, seven ten, king four, jack three, queen two; other cards zero.',
